<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">7 April in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 7 April, from 529 to 1994.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/corpus-juris-civilis" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/corpus-juris-civilis.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">529 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,497 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Justinian promulgates the first Code of Roman law</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Emperor Justinian issued the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/codex-justinianus">Codex Justinianus</a>, gathering imperial constitutions into a single authoritative collection. Revised in 534, it became the core of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/corpus-juris-civilis">Corpus Juris Civilis</a> that shaped European law.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/corpus-juris-civilis">Corpus Juris Civilis</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/codex-justinianus">Codex Justinianus</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-law">Roman law</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1348">1348 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">678 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Charles IV founds the university in Prague</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-iv">Charles IV</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/king-of-bohemia">King of Bohemia</a>, issued the charter founding a university in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prague">Prague</a>, the first in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-europe">Central Europe</a>. Now <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-university">Charles University</a>, it later became a centre of the Hussite reform movement.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/kingdom-of-bohemia">Kingdom of Bohemia</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/king-of-bohemia">King of Bohemia</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-europe">Central Europe</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-iv">Charles IV</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1449">1449 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">577 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Antipope Felix V renounces his claim to the papacy</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Felix V, the former Duke Amadeus VIII of Savoy, renounced his claim to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/papacy">papacy</a>, ending the reign of the last antipope. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/council-of-basel">Council of Basel</a> had elected him in 1439, after he had retired to a hermitage.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amadeus-viii-duke-of-savoy">Amadeus VIII, Duke of Savoy</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/papacy">Papacy</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1739">1739 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">287 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Highwayman Dick Turpin is hanged at York</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Dick Turpin, convicted of horse theft, was hanged on the Knavesmire at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/york">York</a>. The violent robber was later romanticised in fiction as a dashing gentleman of the road.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1798">1798 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">228 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Congress creates the Mississippi Territory</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The US Congress organised the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mississippi-river">Mississippi</a> Territory on land ceded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> in 1795. It was later enlarged and divided into the states of Mississippi and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alabama">Alabama</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1827">1827 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">199 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">John Walker records the first sale of friction matches</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Stockton-on-Tees chemist John Walker sold his newly invented 'friction lights', matches struck against sandpaper. He never patented them, and others soon copied the idea.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1939">1939 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">87 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Italy invades Albania</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benito-mussolini">Mussolini</a>'s forces landed at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/durres">Durrës</a> and other ports, and within days <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zog-i">King Zog</a> had fled. Albania was joined to the Italian crown, and the invasion later served as a base for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>'s attack on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1994">1994 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">32 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Genocide against the Tutsi begins in Rwanda</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Hours after President Habyarimana's aircraft was shot down, extremists began killing Tutsi and moderate <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hutu">Hutu</a>. In about 100 days an estimated 500,000 to 800,000 people were murdered.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genocide">Genocide</a></div></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 7 April <span class="n">5</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/otto-ii-duke-of-bavaria"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/otto-ii-duke-of-bavaria.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Otto II, Duke of Bavaria</span><span class="tp">1206–1253</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/francis-xavier"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/francis-xavier.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Francis Xavier</span><span class="tp">1506–1552</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/gustav-landauer"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/gustav-landauer.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Gustav Landauer</span><span class="tp">1870–1919</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/gabriela-mistral"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/gabriela-mistral.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Gabriela Mistral</span><span class="tp">1889–1957</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/ravi-shankar"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ravi-shankar.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Ravi Shankar</span><span class="tp">1920–2012</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 7 April <span class="n">8</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/berengar-i-of-italy"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/berengar-i-of-italy.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Berengar I of Italy</span><span class="tp">c. 845–924</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/charles-viii-of-france"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/charles-viii-of-france.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Charles VIII of France</span><span class="tp">1470–1498</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/el-greco"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/el-greco.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">El Greco</span><span class="tp">1541–1614</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/lennart-torstensson"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/lennart-torstensson.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Lennart Torstensson</span><span class="tp">1603–1651</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/taksin"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/taksin.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Taksin</span><span class="tp">1734–1782</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/antoni-radziwill"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/antoni-radziwill.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Antoni Radziwiłł</span><span class="tp">1775–1833</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/begum-hazrat-mahal"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/begum-hazrat-mahal.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Begum Hazrat Mahal</span><span class="tp">c. 1820–1879</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/abeid-karume"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/abeid-karume.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Abeid Karume</span><span class="tp">1905–1972</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
